index 5642480eafc84dda78a578366c0b3f165e3a759a..4a9f13679b9ebd6219259cdef9c01a4587b8d1c8 100644
--- a/docs/userguide/configuration.rst
+++ b/docs/userguide/configuration.rst
@@ -625,6 +625,45 @@ Configuring this setting only applies to tasks that are
 acknowledged **after** they have been executed and only if
 :setting:`task_acks_late` is enabled.
 
+.. deprecated:: 6.0
+    Use :setting:`task_acks_on_failure` and :setting:`task_acks_on_timeout`
+    instead. This setting will be removed in 7.0.
+
+.. setting:: task_acks_on_failure
+
+``task_acks_on_failure``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Default: None
+
+When enabled messages for all tasks will be acknowledged even if they
+fail. When disabled, failed messages will be rejected instead.
+
+If not set, this falls back to :setting:`task_acks_on_failure_or_timeout`,
+and ultimately defaults to enabled.
+
+Configuring this setting only applies to tasks that are
+acknowledged **after** they have been executed and only if
+:setting:`task_acks_late` is enabled.
+
+.. setting:: task_acks_on_timeout
+
+``task_acks_on_timeout``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Default: None
+
+When enabled messages for all tasks will be acknowledged even if they
+time out. When disabled, timed-out messages will be rejected and requeued
+instead of being acknowledged.
+
+If not set, this falls back to :setting:`task_acks_on_failure_or_timeout`,
+and ultimately defaults to enabled.
+
+Configuring this setting only applies to tasks that are
+acknowledged **after** they have been executed and only if
+:setting:`task_acks_late` is enabled.
+
 .. setting:: task_reject_on_worker_lost
 
 ``task_reject_on_worker_lost``
